"""gen-reference: the browsable Interleaf reference (spec 002 FR-030, FR-031).

    gen-reference [--out DIR] [--designs STAGE]
                                 write the site (default out/reference); DIR is replaced if it
                                 is new, empty or an earlier build of this tool, else refused

The site is static and every link is relative, so it opens from a file, from a local
server (make serve-reference) and from GitHub Pages under /ui/. It is styled with
Interleaf itself (web/tokens.css, web/bundle.css, copied into DIR/web/) and shows:

    index.html          the guidelines (interleaf/README.md)
    tokens.html         every token: usage, a value per theme, a sample
    components.html     every component: its guidelines and a live preview
    previews/NAME.html  each component's preview.html with the web form loaded
    designs.html        with --designs: the design boards (spec 003 FR-016, FR-017), each
                        folder of STAGE copied to designs/ (tools/site-designs writes STAGE:
                        PROJECT/ for each design on main, pr-N/PROJECT/ and pr-N/pr.json for each
                        open pull request that changes a design), and designs/pr-N/index.html

The picker (voice, scheme, pen) offers the combinations of web/combinations.json and sets
their attributes on the page and, by postMessage, inside every preview. Python stdlib only;
the output has no timestamps, so a build from the same sources is byte for byte the same.
"""
